This Court has perused the impugned judgment, trial court record as well as other material placed on record and we find that the respondent had got herself examined as PW-1 before the learned Family Court and stated on oath that her father-in-law was permanent employee of MCD (East) and was drawing monthly salary of Rs.25,000/- approximately; he had three properties in his name as noted above; her deceased husband was running a shop from property bearing No. B-139;
she was influenced to temporarily shift to property No. B-140 so that property B-140 could be reconstructed; however, she was made to live in a much smaller accommodation and in inhuman conditions. She has also stated that the three shops earlier existing in property B-139 were converted into two shops, thereby, she was left with no shop and also the construction on the first floor comprised only of big hall, without any kitchen and bathroom, which her mother-in-law used as Bhagwan Das vs Sunita on 12 December, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/44285490/
4 dumping room.
